      "message": "Can we separate the condition in a few booleans so that it makes more sense but also add comments so that readers in the future don\u0027t get confused as to what\u0027s going on? This works because of a lot of factors that are non-trivial.\n\n - We need to special case because ExternalTextures may end up using two planes of the same YUV texture.\n   - This cannot happen in OpenGL that actually needs the validation of texture views matching so it\u0027s safe for backends to ignore this here.\n   - The formats may not match because the Y and UV planes have different format counts.\n - We don\u0027t allow creating multiplanar texture views directly in WebGPU so this code cannot be triggered on purpose by JS and instead is only hit when Chromium creates a YUV texture itself.\n \nBut IMHO we could more simply change `TextureViewsAllMatch` to check `TextureViewsMatch` first and then if that fails still `continue` if `first` is multiplanar, with a comment explaining why we special case. This makes the special case more clear.",
